480 - Dear Lord and Father
 / 
Key: Eb
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 480
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[Eb]Dear Lord and Father of [Bb]mankind,
[Eb]Forgive [Gm]our [Ddim]foolish [Bb]ways;
[Bb]Reclothe [Cm]us [Fm/C]in [Eb]our [Ddim]rightful [Gm]mind,
[Fm]Inpurer [Cm]lives [Fm]Thy [Gm]service [Bb]find,
[Bb]In deeper reverence, [Gm]praise,
[Bb7]In deeper [Ab/C]reverence, [Eb]praise.

Verse 2:
[Eb]In simple trust like theirs [Bb]who heard,
[Eb]beside [Gm]the [Ddim]Syrian [Bb]sea,
[Bb]the [Cm]gracious [Fm/C]calling [Ddim]of [Ab]the [Gm]Lord,
[Bb]let us, [Eb]like [Bb]them, without [Gm]a word,
[Bb7]rise [Ab]up and [Eb/Bb]follow thee.

Verse 3:
[Eb]O sabbath rest by Galilee,
[Eb]O [Ab]calm [Gm]of [Ddim]hills [Eb]above,
[Bb]where [Cm]Jesus [Fm/C]knelt [Eb]to [Ddim]share [Ab]with [Gm]thee
[Bb]the silence of eternity,
[Bb7]interpreted [Ab]by [Eb]love!

Verse 4:
[Eb]Drop thy still dews of [Bb]quietness,
[Eb]till [Ab]all [Gm]our [Ddim]strivings [Bb]cease;
[Bb]take [Cm]from our [Fm/C]souls [Eb]the [Ddim]strain [Ab]and [Gm]stress,
[Bb]and let [Eb]our [Bb]ordered lives [Gm]confess
[Bb7]the [Ab]beauty [Eb/Bb]of [Ab]thy [Eb]peace.

Verse 5:
[Eb]Breathe through the heats of our [Bb]desire
[Eb]thy [Ab]coolness [Ddim]and [Eb]thy [Bb]balm;
[Bb]let [Cm]sense be [Fm/C]dumb, [Eb]let [Ddim]flesh [Ab]retire;
[Bb]speak through [Eb]the [Bb]earthquake, wind, [Gm]and fire,
[Bb7]O [Ab]still, small [Eb/Bb]voice [Ab]of [Eb]calm.
